<title>DENMARK: EAC to market snacks with Orkla.</title>
<headline>EAC to market snacks with Orkla.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish shipping and trading group East Asiatic Company (EAC) said on Friday that it had agreed to join Norway's Orkla in a joint venture selling snack products in Asia.</p>
<p>An EAC statement said that the partners would each own 50 percent of a new company, KiMs Asia, which would produce KiMs -brand snacks in Malaysia and market them there and elsewhere.</p>
<p>&quot;KiMs Asia will focus, in the first instance, on Malaysia and Singapore but will later expand to other selected markets in Asia,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>Production, it added, would take place on new equipment installed in existing premises. --Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
